{
  "source_id": "state-about",
  "text": "About the Election Results Dashboard | NCSBE\nSkip to main content\nThe General Election is Nov. 3\nCheck Your Voter Registration:\nUse the Voter Search Tool\nDid you recently receive a letter about your voter registration?\nFind answers to your questions in our FAQ.\nRead More\nRegistration Repair Project\nCheck if your N.C. voter registration is incomplete, learn how to fix it, and find more information in the FAQ:\nRegistration Repair\nPrevious\nPause\nPlay\nNext\nAn official website of the State of North Carolina\nAn official website of NC\nHow you know\nState Government websites value user privacy. To learn more,\nview our full privacy policy\n.\nSecure websites use HTTPS certificates. A lock icon or https:// means you\u2019ve safely connected to the official website.\nUtility Menu\nAbout\nContact\nMedia\nnc.gov\nMain menu\nRegistering\nRegistering\nHow to Register\nWho Can Register\nUpdating Registration\nChecking Your Registration\nChoosing Your Party Affiliation\nHosting Voter Registration Drives\nNational Voter Registration Act (NVRA)\nFAQ: Voter Registration\nVoting\nVoting\nUpcoming Election\nYour Voter Record\nVoter ID\nVote Early in Person\nVote in Person on Election Day\nVote By Mail\nMilitary and Overseas Voting\nHelp for Voters with Disabilities\nProvisional Voting\nVoter Tools & Forms\nVoting Technology\nVote in Honor of a Veteran\nFor Candidates\nFor Candidates\nRunning for Office\nFiling for Candidacy\nTerms of Office\nCandidate Challenges\nWithdrawal of Candidacy\nPetitions\nResults & Data\nResults & Data\nElection Results\nVoter Registration Data\nCandidate Lists\nAbsentee and Provisional Data\nVoter Turnout\nPolling Place Data\nVoter History Data\nVoting Maps/Redistricting\nCampaign Finance\nCampaign Finance\nRequest for Proposals\nSearch Campaign Funding and Spending Reports\nReporting Schedules\nTreasurer Training\nReporting Software\nReporting Forms\nCandidate Committees\nOther Political Committees\nFederal Political Committees\nIndependent Expenditures, Electioneering Communications and Special Contributors\nReferendum Committees\nLimitation on Fund-Raising During Legislative Session\nDisclosure Legends\nCampaign Finance Audits and Investigations\nPenalties\nCampaign Finance Advisory Opinions\nAbout Elections\nAbout Elections\nCounty Boards of Elections\nElection Security\nLegal Resources\nMaintaining Accurate Voter Rolls\nGet Involved in Elections\nTypes of Elections\nElectoral College\nCareers in Elections\nUtility Menu\nAbout\nContact\nMedia\nnc.gov\nSearch\nHome\nResults & Data\nElection Results\nAbout the Election Results Dashboard\nOn election night, stay up-to-date with our\nElection Results Dashboard\n, where you can:\nView live election results, updated every 5\u201310 minutes after all polls close.\nExplore data via breakout maps, tables, and charts.\nDownload election results data spreadsheets.\nAccess historical election results (1992\u2013present).\nWhen is the dashboard updated on election night?\nOnce polls close on election night, the dashboard is updated every 5\u201310 minutes as precincts report results to the State Board of Elections.\nHow do I use the dashboard?\nTo view election results, follow these steps:\nGo to the\nDashboard\n.\nSelect the desired Election Date; County (for statewide results select \u201cState\u201d); Office; and Contest.\nClick \u201cDisplay Results.\u201d\nDon\u2019t forget to click \u201cRefresh\u201d to view the most recent results.\nExample to view the 2024 presidential election results on election night:\nGo to the Dashboard.\nMake the following selections:\nElection: 11/05/2024\nCounty: State\nOffice: Federal\nContest: US President\nClick \u201cDisplay Results.\u201d\nTo explore the election results further:\nPerform the steps listed above.\nClick\nView Contest Details\n(right side of page, in dark blue bar).\nThe\nContest Details\ntab provides the total number of votes received by each candidate or ballot item, along with a map showing the winner of each county.\nThe\nResults by Voting Method\ntab provides a table with a breakdown of votes cast by method (e.g., in-person on election day, absentee by mail, etc.).\nThe\nResults by Contest\ntab provides a table with a breakdown of votes cast in each county.\nDon\u2019t forget to click \u201cRefresh\u201d to view the most recent results.\nOn This Page Jump Links\nOff\nSide Nav\nElection Results\nAbout the Election Results Dashboard\nElection Night Reporting Timeline\nUS President and NC Governor\nHistorical Election Results Data\nContact\nNorth Carolina State Board of Elections (NCSBE)\nP.O. Box 27255\nRaleigh, NC 27611-7255\nEmail:\nelections.sboe@ncsbe.gov\nPhone:\n(919) 814-0700\nFax: (919) 715-0135\nFollow Us\nFacebook Posts\nNC State Board of Elections\nCounty Boards Resources\nResources for County Boards\nNCSBE Public Files (FTP)\nVoter Tools\nVoter Search\nCounty Boards of Elections Search\nBallotTrax (Absentee Ballot Tracking)\nVoter Registration Statistics\nView all tools and forms\nWork With Us\nCareer Opportunities\nVoter Information\nUse of Partial Social Security Numbers\nNetwork Menu\nnc.gov\nWebsite Feedback\nAccessibility\nDisclaimer & Terms of Use\nPrivacy Policy\nOpen Budget\nHosted on Digital Commons",
